cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "grader-variance: an Inspect-native measurement of how much of a benchmark score is the grader"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ciesielski
    given-names: Joanna
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2397-3660"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joanna-ciesielski/grader-variance"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An extension for the Inspect evaluation framework that isolates LLM-grader
  (judge) variance from model-sampling variance, decomposes the spread in a
  benchmark's score into question, model-sampling, and grader components, and
  provides a stopping rule for how many grader repeats are needed. Grader
  self-inconsistency is established prior art (Rating Roulette, arXiv 2510.27106;
  Reliability without Validity, arXiv 2606.19544); the contribution here is the
  variance decomposition of the grader term and its repeat-count stopping rule,
  stated in the form of Miller's "Adding Error Bars to Evals" (arXiv 2411.00640),
  delivered as a native Inspect extension. Statistics are computed by the
  rater-agreement library (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21983269).
keywords:
  - inspect
  - llm-as-judge
  - evaluation
  - grader-variance
  - variance-decomposition
  - intra-rater-reliability
